      <Comment source="pmngroup">The APX1 ascorbate peroxidase is predicted to be a cytosolic enzyme that plays a crucial role in reducing |FRAME: HYDROGEN-PEROXIDE| levels in Arabidopsis leaves |CITS: [12694594][15608336]|. In general, ascorbate peroxidases produce the |FRAME: CPD-318| radical, but this can undergo spontaneous disproportionation to produce |FRAME: L-DEHYDRO-ASCORBATE| |CITS: [NAKANO87]|.</Comment>
